  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two scans; recent head for latency",
      "items": [
        "The first scan covers the configured lookback and fixes its cutoff.",
        "Arrivals have their own frozen interval, cursor and completed-through watermark.",
        "A newer head page cannot overwrite either scan\u2019s continuation. All candidate IDs are recorded before checkpoints advance.",
        "Per poll: at most one head page, one backlog page, one arrivals page; 25 IDs per page.",
        "Up to 25 queued read retries and 1\u20135 admitted executions per poll; defaults execute one request."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What reaches the model",
      "items": [
        "Latest plain-text body request, exact verified attachment Stash references, enabled tool results and this sender\u2019s last three completed exchanges.",
        "Attachments are data, not action permissions. Filenames/types/sizes are context; binary contents are not injected into the prompt.",
        "Operator memories, auto-context, shared Intelligence reads/writes and conversation logging are disabled.",
        "Model/provider choice still follows the configured mode. Tool RAG ranking and normal private diagnostic logs remain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Persistence and failure boundaries",
      "items": [
        "Ledger and settings live on the Jarvis host: data/email-inbox/<account-hash>/ledger.sqlite3. No Memory DB migration.",
        "Private contacts and ledger are Git-ignored and excluded from image builds.",
        "Named files use the existing Workspace/Stash bridge after admission. Raw EML remains temporary; Stash uses normal project retention.",
        "read_failed records IDs, reasons and attempt counts after three failed reads; other requests continue.",
        "Malformed / unauthorized MIME \u2192 ignored. A saved answer can send even when scanning fails.",
        "Unconfirmed send \u2192 needs_attention, no automatic resend. Completed requests never automatically rerun.",
        "The status command reads local policy and ledger without starting Gmail or checking remote health."
      ]
    }
  ]
